data: {"id":"chatcmpl-f962cf82-0a29-413b-84dd-cf8b18994d21","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1790744723,"model":"capitoline-judge-sol61","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"In a three-node Nutanix cluster, **RF2 stores two copies of each data block on different nodes**. If one node fails, the cluster normally remains operational and data remains accessible. However, blocks with a replica on the failed node now have only one surviving copy; blocks replicated across the two surviving nodes retain both copies.\n\n**Nutanix can automatically rebuild the missing replicas onto the two remaining nodes**, provided sufficient free storage capacity is available. It does not have to wait for the failed node to return or for a replacement node to be added to restore two copies of the data.\n\nRestoring data redundancy does **not** restore full cluster fault tolerance. The surviving nodes retain the required majority quorum, but another node failure would remove that quorum and make the cluster unavailable, even after rebuilding completes. Restoring or replacing the third node returns the cluster to full single-node failure tolerance."},"finish_reason":null}]}

